'''Ramiq''' ([[Qymish language|Qymish]]: Ⱃⰰⰿⰹⱒ) is a [[Qym]]ish aerospace and defense [[wikipedia:crown corporation|crown corporation]]. 

==History==

==Budget and management==
Ramiq is operated as an independent crown corporation and receives a subsidy from the [[Royal Ministry of Defense (Qym)|Royal Ministry of Defense]] for research and development. Unlike [[Vajdila]], which has a domestic and export mission, Ramiq has solely a domestic mission with a prohibition to sell any of its products to any entity other than the [[Government of Qym]]. 

==Products==
*Fighters
**[[Ramiq R-20]] (4th generation fighter; similar to the [[wikipedia:Mikoyan MiG-29|Mikoyan MiG-29]])
**[[Ramiq R-22]] (4th generation interceptor; similar to the [[wikipedia:Mikoyan MiG-31|Mikoyan MiG-31]])
**[[Ramiq R-26]] (5th generation stealth air superiority; similar to the [[wikipedia:Chengdu J-20|Chengdu J-20]])
*Bombers
**[[Ramiq T-55]] (strategic bomber; similar to the [[wikipedia:Rockwell B-1 Lancer|Rockwell B-1 Lancer]])
**[[Ramiq T-66]] (stealth bomber; similar to the [[wikipedia:Northrop B-2 Spirit|Northrop B-2 Spirit]])
*Trainer
**[[Ramiq C-8K]]
**[[Ramiq C-9K]]
**[[Ramiq C-10K]]
*UAVs
**[[Ramiq K-703]]
**[[Ramiq K-707]]
**[[Ramiq K-1000]]
**[[Ramiq K-1200]]
**[[Ramiq K-1400]]
**[[Ramiq Sh-12]]

